=== parameters ===
P4 WEAK panel subsample n_assets=50; HORIZON=5; N_FOLDS=5; EMBARGO=5
TB: AFML ch.3 vol-scaled bands pt=sl=k*sigma_t with k=1.0, sigma=lagged EWMA span=20
PRIMARY metric: mean daily cross-sectional RankIC (+ t-stat / ICIR)
pooled Spearman is a COUNTEREXAMPLE (mixes time-series + cross-sectional variation)
cite: López de Prado AFML ch.3 (vol-scaled barriers), ch.7 (purged CV)
look-ahead: features ≤ t; sigma_t = EWMA.shift(1); labels walk t+1..; purge on label-span overlap
MU_WEAK=0.001 panel (750, 50)
rows=36300 features=['mom_1', 'mom_5', 'mom_10', 'mom_20', 'vol_20', 'vol_5', 'rank_mom20']

=== label construction look-ahead audit ===
fwd_ret[t] = sum(rets[t+1..t+h])
TB: pt=sl=1.0*sigma_t per asset/time; sigma from lagged EWMA — NOT fixed 2%
why fixed 2% is wrong: high-vol names hit barriers by noise; low-vol almost never touch → labels become vol-driven
